= Open science — Technical =

Open-science systems combine policy, licensing, repositories, persistent identifiers, metadata, interoperable formats, transparent workflows, and community governance. Openness improves inspectability and reuse opportunities but does not by itself establish data quality, methodological validity, or reproducibility.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* open science ≠ open access only
* open science ≠ all research must be public without limits
* openness ≠ reproducibility automatically

